! Expression-based laser ramper with z-sweep capability
! DM validation run: LASER_XI ramped to 0.3556232088098463 during ON (was 0.1
! for the original 10.6 um CO2 LCFA reference) -- this is the value giving
! chi_e = 0.002 at 1064 nm, theta=10 deg, E=45.6 GeV (see ../README.md).
! Pattern: 100 turns ON, 1 turn OFF, repeat cyclically (unchanged from reference).
! During ON: sweep LASER_Z_CENTER across electron bunch (unchanged from reference).
!
! Uses modulo function to create periodic square wave and linear sweep
! NOTE (unchanged from the original reference file): the "at 18 GeV" label on
! turn_time below is stale/inherited from an earlier RCS-era version of this
! ramper script. The VALUE itself (3.023586e-4 s) is correct for this ring --
! it equals C/c = 90644.836 m / (2.99792458e8 m/s), the actual FCC-ee Z
! revolution period, and it does feed into on_time/cycle_time, which the
! ON/OFF and sweep expressions below use. Verified before reuse here; left
! as found rather than editing the validated reference's comment text.

! === TIMING PARAMETERS ===
turn_time = 3.023586E-04  ! seconds per turn at 18 GeV
on_turns = 100
off_turns = 1
cycle_turns = on_turns + off_turns  ! Total turns per cycle
on_time = on_turns * turn_time      ! 1.281337 ms
cycle_time = cycle_turns * turn_time ! 14.0947 ms

! === RF AND BUNCH PARAMETERS ===
C = 90644.836       ! circumference in m
h = 121200            ! RF harmonic number
phi0 = 0.6779       ! RF phase in rad (from lat.bmad)
lambda_RF = C / h   ! RF wavelength = 0.506507 m

! Bunch center from empirical formula: z_center = 4 × φ₀ × λ_RF / (2π)
z_center = 47.85e-3 ! 4 * phi0 * lambda_RF / (2 * pi)  ! ≈ 0.2186 m

sig_z = 2.0e-3      ! bunch RMS length in m (from init file)
sweep_range = 3 * sig_z  ! sweep ±3σ_z = ±6 mm around center

! === LASER INTENSITY RAMPER (ON/OFF CONTROL) ===
! Expression:
! - modulo(time, cycle_time) gives time within current cycle (0 to cycle_time)
! - (on_time - modulo(...)) is positive during ON period, negative during OFF period
! - Divide by cycle_time to get small number, then ceiling():
!   * During ON: ceiling(small positive) = 1
!   * During OFF: ceiling(small negative) = 0
! - Multiply by the peak LASER_XI value (0.3556232088098463 here; see README.md)

ramp_laser_xi: ramper = {laser_ip[LASER_XI]: 0.3556232088098463 * ceiling((on_time - modulo(time, cycle_time)) / cycle_time)}, &
               var = {time}

! === LASER Z-CENTER RAMPER (SWEEP CONTROL) ===
! During ON period: sweep linearly from (z_center - 3σ_z) to (z_center + 3σ_z)
! During OFF period: return to z_center
!
! Sweep formula:
!   is_on = ceiling((on_time - modulo(time, cycle_time)) / cycle_time)
!   sweep_fraction = modulo(time, cycle_time) / on_time  (0 to 1 during ON)
!   z = z_center + is_on * sweep_range * (2 * sweep_fraction - 1)
!
! This gives:
!   - At start of ON (t=0): z = z_center - sweep_range
!   - At end of ON (t=on_time): z = z_center + sweep_range
!   - During OFF: z = z_center (is_on = 0)

ramp_laser_z: ramper = {laser_ip[LASER_Z_CENTER]: z_center + &
                        sweep_range * (2 * modulo(time, cycle_time) / on_time - 1) * &
                        ceiling((on_time - modulo(time, cycle_time)) / cycle_time)}, &
              var = {time}
